{"kind":"request","text":"DX-T1 (recut): typed definition package, the live Counter and lending\nre-expressed. Replaces da58095a; amended by request 1761d819.\n\nBuild the package that lets an author write a declared definition as\ntyped TypeScript which compiles to exactly the data the scope pins.\nChild of request 99c4756a; the spike is branch\nspike/typed-definitions-20261028 at 6fed3495, directory\nspikes/typed-definitions, whose REPORT.md has the measurements and\nlimits. The spike's lib.ts is the core.\n\nThe package's design rule, from 1761d819 item 3, four forms:\n- Builders compile into the pinned bytes: every contract form, in this\n  head the forms below and in DX-T3 the rest.\n- Derivations are computed from the value and never authored: the pin,\n  projection field types, forms, acts by state, expected revisions, act\n  sentences, input schemas, documentation tables.\n- Annotations are typed sidecars keyed by the definition's literal names\n  and compiled into the package presentation, never into the pin.\n- Code is typed by the definition. Platform definitions, the membership\n  role lists, the destination and rules scopes are referenced by type\n  and never authored.\nDownstream readers keep reading the pinned bytes; none of them takes a\nTypeScript dependency.\n\nWanted:\n1. Package @generalbusiness/dap-define at packages/define, with the\n   builders: field types, slots, item, open, transition, comment,\n   timed, define, guards and effects typed by item, range, tell and the\n   other sends, when, and compile returning the canonical digest and\n   the builder's findings; plus unset, anyOf, before and settles, which\n   the live Counter uses; define accepts level and capacity. Shallow\n   types only: const type parameters and keyof. The findings scan of\n   direct rule references stays until DX-T2 adds the tagged template.\n2. The lending library and the live Counter, apps/counter/commitments.json\n   (counting-commitments, digest b5582434), re-expressed with the\n   package, pins unchanged. The spike's counting rewrite (435d9f57)\n   stays as a witness. The JSON stays beside the source, and a CI check\n   fails when regeneration does not reproduce a pin byte for byte.\n3. Documentation in docs/write-an-application.md: the typed form as a\n   way to write a definition, the four forms, the data stays the unit\n   of trust. Plain English, lines at most 79 characters, no\n   comparisons.\n4. The witness: the regeneration check run on main's pins, and the\n   spike's nine name mistakes reproduced as compile errors.\n\nThe kernel is unchanged and no filing-gate item is opened. The spike\ndirectory is not landed; the package replaces it.","body":{"conditions":"One gate, exact-head checker review, PD-2 note with the witness.","target_head":"06e4d33fe17937610891f29b5d1513b9e224edea","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3","to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}